content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-107 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22950",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Current vibration: 5.5 mm/s RMS at the drive-end bearing housing falls within Figure 3 Zone C (4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS), classified 'Restricted - plan maintenance'. It is below the Zone D boundary of 7.1 mm/s RMS, so the documented immediate-stop condition does not apply to this reading. Figure 3 is the applicable HF-300 limit for velocity measured on bearing housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration trend: last month's 3.0 mm/s RMS was in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'). The increase to 5.5 mm/s RMS is 2.5 mm/s RMS and moves the reported reading from Zone B to Zone C.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: 76°C on the drive-end housing is 6°C above the manual's normal limit of 70°C, but below the 80°C alarm and 90°C trip limits. The comparison is applicable because the manual specifies bearing-housing surface temperature. Consequently, the report shows elevated temperature but does not meet the site rule for a priority-1 work order, which applies above the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Work-order decision: assign P2 planned corrective maintenance because the current vibration is in Zone C and temperature is above normal. Neither documented emergency trigger is currently met: vibration is not in the highest severity zone and temperature is below the alarm and trip values. Zone C does not provide a specific completion deadline.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: none is reported. The troubleshooting table links leakage at the shaft seal with mechanical-seal replacement; no such leakage symptom is present, and the high-vibration/high-temperature rows do not independently establish a seal-replacement scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is a leading, unconfirmed hypothesis because it is a documented cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature. Confirm by bearing inspection and checking for noise.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment is another leading, unconfirmed hypothesis because it can cause both reported symptoms. Check it with laser alignment rather than assuming bearing failure.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing can explain the high bearing temperature; check grease quantity before attributing the temperature solely to bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage can explain the high vibration; inspect the impeller during internal examination.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation is a further documented cause of high vibration; check NPSH. No NPSH or cavitation evidence is supplied in the report.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before repair, measure and record vibration velocity on both bearing housings, not only the drive end. Classify the highest reading using Figure 3 and recheck the drive-end housing surface temperature against the 70°C normal, 80°C alarm and 90°C trip values.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the combined symptoms before replacing parts: check drive-end bearing grease quantity, check for bearing noise or wear indications, and check NPSH for possible cavitation. Record the findings; the evidence does not provide grease-quantity or NPSH acceptance values.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-check shaft alignment and record parallel offset and angular error. The documented alignment tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular error.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For internal inspection or repair, isolate and drain the pump and apply the isolation, line-break and lifting controls listed below. Remove the back pull-out assembly for access; its rotating assembly can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework, but the assembly itself weighs 68 kg and requires lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and impeller. If bearing replacement is triggered because either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: HF3-512 drive-end 6312-C3 and HF3-510 non-drive-end 6310-C3. Do not replace only the drive-end bearing. Inspect the impeller for imbalance or damage before deciding whether any impeller part is needed.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, use lightly oiled threads and tighten disturbed fasteners to Table 5: bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm if the impeller was removed; and casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm if those joints were disturbed. If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser alignment and restore the tolerances of 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular error.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before closing the work order, record vibration on both housings and the bearing-housing temperatures. Continue weekly vibration monitoring and classify the highest reading. If a reading falls in Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if temperature rises above the 80°C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; provisional for the bearing-repair scope and to be used as one of the pair if either bearing requires replacement for wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; provisional for the bearing-repair scope and required together with the drive-end bearing when pair replacement is triggered.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; conditional on the casing being opened, because the parts list requires replacement whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, drain and vent first, and obtain a line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the site's 25 kg lifting threshold. Use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The present 5.5 mm/s RMS reading is not in Zone D. If subsequent measurement on either housing falls in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The present 76°C reading is below the 80°C alarm. If bearing temperature rises above the manufacturer's alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the pump remains in service, maintain the documented Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm whether the line is chemically dosed before line break. Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required for work on chemically dosed lines; the report does not establish the fluid service.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician. Apply this to the alignment task; any additional diagnostic or repeat-alignment duration must be confirmed separately rather than assumed.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair, if executed: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and expressly prohibits fitting HF3-450 on those pumps. P-107 is serial HF3-22950 and is therefore within the bulletin scope. For any seal replacement added to this work order, use pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B; the manual option for pumps below HF3-22000 does not apply. No sleeve measurement is needed for the pre-set seal, and sleeve HF3-455 must be replaced if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal-gland nuts, whereas the applicable bulletin specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B on this serial range. Therefore 30 Nm governs if HF3-450B is fitted on P-107; the manual's 25 Nm value must not be used for that seal. This is a conditional control for added seal work, not a finding that the current no-leakage report requires seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the current non-drive-end vibration reading? Only the drive-end value is reported, but monitoring requires measurement on both housings and classification of the highest reading. [C06]",
    "What are the actual bearing condition/noise, grease quantity, alignment measurements, impeller condition and NPSH results? These findings are needed to distinguish among the documented causes and decide whether bearing replacement is required. [C09, C10]",
    "What grease specification and correct grease quantity apply, and what NPSH test method and acceptance value should the technician use? The troubleshooting table calls for these checks but the evidence supplies no values or procedures. [C09]",
    "Is the pump line chemically dosed, requiring chemical goggles and nitrile gloves, and what additional fluid-specific precautions are needed before line break? The service fluid is not identified. [C15]",
    "Will the internal inspection require casing opening or any seal disturbance? This determines whether the conditional casing gasket and bulletin-compliant seal parts/procedure are needed; the present report does not establish that scope. [C05, C09, C13]",
    "What completion date is required for the Zone C restriction, and what standard labour applies to diagnosis, isolation and lifting? Zone C says to plan maintenance but gives no deadline, and Table 6 provides no times for those supporting activities. [C07, C12]"
  ]
}
